<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intellĕgĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		intellego. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That can be understood</i>, <i>intelligible</i>, <i>intellectual</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bonum (opp. intellegibile),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 124, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Soliloq. 1, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Perceptible</i> to the senses, <i>sensible</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in corporis intellegibilis lineam (dyas) prima
					defluxit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 6, 19</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intellĕgĭlĭter</span></b> , <i>intelligibly</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. Ep.
				218</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
